    "title": "Pretty New Color Schemes Coming To PlayStation 5 Soon - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Zak Wojnar ,\n11 hours ago\nFor many players, simply having a PlayStation 5 and accompanying DualSense controllers is enough. But others prefer a more personal touch. For those users, there are a variety of console skins and controller variants from which to choose, and now, there are even more options.\nIn a PlayStation Blog post, Sony announced the \"Hyperpop Collection,\" a trio of new looks for the PS5 and DualSense controller. The new options include \"Techno Red,\" \"Remix Green,\" and \"Rhythm Blue.\" All three variants have the same basic design, with the top of the console/controller being black but quickly fading to the bold new color.\nThey look great, but it's odd that they only seem to be available for the PlayStation 5 slim variant. It looks like there's no option for the PS5 Pro or the original 'husky' PlayStation 5. Likewise, it's bizarre that only the DualSense controller is supported, rather than the premium DualSense Edge.\nNevertheless, I think the Hyperpop Collection looks great. I'm fine with my current setup, but that Rhythm Blue certainly looks gorgeous! Plus, I don't actually have the PS5 Slim. I only have the original chunky model and a PS5 Pro. If they had a DualSense Edge version of these colors, maybe I'd give indulge in an impulse buy, but I've got enough controllers (seriously, as something of a collector, I probably have too many!)\nAnyway, these new accessories will be available starting March 12, 2026, with pre-orders beginning from January 16.\nRelated: Love PlayStation Games? Try PlayStation Shoes!\n1",
